 "notes": "Found by First Read on the address '375 Glen Drive': the City's property address '375 Glen Drive, Vancouver, BC (City of Vancouver property address, Strathcona)'. Zoning district CD-1 (819) (CD-1 by-law 819) from the City's zoning districts dataset at that point. A CD-1 district has no general schedule: its limits are in CD-1 by-law No. 819. Lot area 1,941.7 m² from the parcel polygon (4 vertices, not a rectangle: the frontage and depth are an equivalent rectangle with the same area); frontage taken as the side along Glen Drive from OpenStreetMap, 36.2 m away. A corner lot: E Hastings St also runs beside it, 33.3 m from the centre. The frontage is taken on Glen Drive (34.6 m); the front could instead be the 56.1 m side on E Hastings St Confirm which side is the front: it sets the yards, the envelope and the massing. Four sides but not square-cornered (86% of its 60.4 x 37.2 m bounding rectangle), 1,942 m2. The massing uses the polygon itself: the setback envelope follows the lot lines and the plate is the largest rectangle inside it. Transit-oriented area, the Community Vision map, water and sewer, trees and the owner are not in these datasets: answer them, or leave them 'not sure'. Answers added by hand for the 17 Nov 2026 demonstration: owner City of Vancouver (Daily Hive, 17 Feb 2021); not a former Community Vision area (the site is inside the Downtown Eastside Plan area; confirm on the City's map); transit-oriented area No (no SkyTrain station within 800 m; confirm on the City's TOA map); frequent bus stop Yes (E Hastings St; confirm against TransLink's frequent transit network). Site area set by hand to 2,134.4 m2: the draft CD-1 by-law (s.5.1) says the floor space ratio must be computed on the site as it was at the rezoning application, before any dedications. The City's parcel today is 1,941.7 m2, the figure the lookup found; the referral report requires a 5 m dedication to CN Rail along the western property line, which accounts for the difference. The parcel polygon is today's, so the massing warns that it is smaller than the recorded area. The report gives the lot as about 50 m on Hastings St and 37 m on Glen Drive, with no trees on the site or the street, and Hastings St as Frequent Transit Network. area_plan set by hand to downtown_eastside: the referral report places the site in the Hastings East sub-area of the Downtown Eastside Plan.",
